[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2011086176","html_url":"https://github.com/935963004/LaBraM/issues/8#issuecomment-2011086176","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/8","id":2011086176,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLF0fBs533r1g","user":{"login":"935963004","id":38138106,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MTM4MTA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38138106?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004","html_url":"https://github.com/935963004","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-03-21T02:41:10Z","updated_at":"2024-03-21T02:41:10Z","body":"Thanks for your interest. In my implementation, I generate multiple hdf5 files for different channel numbers. For example, all EEG data with 19 channels are transformed into one hdf5 file while EEG data with 23 channels are transformed into another hdf5 file.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2011086176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2017061157","html_url":"https://github.com/935963004/LaBraM/issues/8#issuecomment-2017061157","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/8","id":2017061157,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLF0fBs54Oekl","user":{"login":"ddicee","id":30242033,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMjQyMDMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30242033?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddicee","html_url":"https://github.com/ddicee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddicee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddicee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddicee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddicee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddicee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddicee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddicee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddicee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddicee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-03-25T01:41:07Z","updated_at":"2024-03-25T01:41:07Z","body":"Thanks a lot for your answer. I'm training the VQNSP using the default configurations as described in the readme, but noticing that the quant_loss keeps increasing while the total loss is decreasing. Just wonder if you have ever seen something like this before. Would you consider this as normal?\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1384\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/935963004/LaBraM/assets/30242033/d6ca05e4-957f-4ee2-8fe0-af19321d2742\">\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2017061157/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2018023797","html_url":"https://github.com/935963004/LaBraM/issues/8#issuecomment-2018023797","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/8","id":2018023797,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLF0fBs54SJl1","user":{"login":"935963004","id":38138106,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MTM4MTA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38138106?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004","html_url":"https://github.com/935963004","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-03-25T13:35:54Z","updated_at":"2024-03-25T13:35:54Z","body":"This is a normal phenomenon. The quant_loss will first increase and then converge to a stable value (about 0.02 in my case). However, the total loss will be always decreasing. So, don't worry about it.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2018023797/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2601412079","html_url":"https://github.com/935963004/LaBraM/issues/8#issuecomment-2601412079","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/8","id":2601412079,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLF0fBs6bDmXv","user":{"login":"TheNorthS","id":79570748,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NTcwNzQ4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79570748?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheNorthS","html_url":"https://github.com/TheNorthS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheNorthS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheNorthS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheNorthS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheNorthS/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheNorthS/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheNorthS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheNorthS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheNorthS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheNorthS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-20T05:37:22Z","updated_at":"2025-01-20T05:37:22Z","body":"> Hi Weibang,\n> \n> 感谢您分享您的出色工作！有一件事我不太清楚。在预处理像 TUEP 这样的数据集时，其中通道数范围从 19 到 23，您如何处理这种变化，以便可以将不同的样本分批并转储到 hdf5 文件中以供以后使用？\n> \n> 提前致谢。\n\nRuntimeError: stack expects each tensor to be equal size, but got [31, 2000] at entry 0 and [27, 2000] at entry 2\n\nI also saved different channels as different files, but the above error occurred during training. Have you encountered this? Could you please explain?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2601412079/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2601464136","html_url":"https://github.com/935963004/LaBraM/issues/8#issuecomment-2601464136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/8","id":2601464136,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLF0fBs6bDzFI","user":{"login":"ddicee","id":30